windowClimbT -- the climb (SEQ 764, 2026-11-23; Tony's rulings via Clay): an only-room field is not selectable, the selection
climbs to the first selectable field, both climbs cross a held form's top into its host, and a closed window's form loses
its selection. Tester's shape, a delta of windowSelectT. No window is shown.
C-1  firstLight: the heading is clicked (selected, its left edge midBlue). Then the empty field left of OK, space, is
     clicked -- the click Tony made: space, bar and firstLight are all only room, so nothing is selected, the heading is
     still outlined, and the window is the same pixel for pixel.
C-2  a click on describeHead, in descriptions held in firstLight: it fires nothing on the way up through 7 fields --
     describeHead, first, wrap, body, descriptions, then inside and firstLight, the host's (5 until this stroke: the
     climb stopped at descriptions).
C-3  ccHost holds ccHeld in ccIn. A click on ccRoom, only room two levels down inside the held form (under ccWrap: a field
     directly under a held form's top climbs into the host by itself, a deeper one reaches the held top and needs the
     crossing -- measured, SEQ 764): the selection climbs through ccWrap and ccHeld's top into the host and lands on ccIn (selectable: it has an onClick and a description), which is described in the host's
     help box; the firing climb crosses too and fires ccIn's onClick, handed ccIn. ccTop is not outlined. ccIn's own
     OUTLINE IS OVER THE HELD FORM (Tony, 2026-11-23, SEQ 765): the pixels are ccIn's left edge before the click (the held
     form's white), ccTop's edge (green), ccIn's edge after (midBlue), and the held form's middle (white: only the outline
     is drawn over it). Until SEQ 765 the outline was drawn before the held form and its fill covered it.
     (descriptions as held in firstLight has NO room a point can land on -- 240 points scanned, all on its four text and
     image fields -- so this form stands in for it.)
C-4  ccBare: only room everywhere. A click on its one field and a click on the form itself: nothing selected, nothing fired.
C-5  the heading selected again; the window closed and opened again: nothing is selected (the heading's edge is the page's
     wall again and no describe line follows). ccHost, never closed and laid out again, still describes ccIn.
